{"subjectId":"dsa-basics","id":"circular_linked","title":"Circular Linked List","group":"Linked Lists","order":12,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">A circular linked list is a singly linked list whose <strong>last node points back to the head</strong> instead of to <code>None</code>. There is no end, so the list can be traversed from any node, and keeping a single pointer gives O(1) access to both the first and the last element.</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--def\"><p><strong>Circular linked list</strong> — a linked list in which the <code>next</code> of the last node refers to the first node. A one-node list points to itself. Traversal stops when we return to the node where we started, not when <code>next</code> is <code>None</code> — because it never is.</p></div>\n<figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>10 → 5 → 20 → 15 → back to 10</figcaption><pre><code>head\n ↓\n┌──────┬────┐    ┌──────┬────┐    ┌──────┬────┐    ┌──────┬────┐\n│  10  │ ●──┼───▶│   5  │ ●──┼───▶│  20  │ ●──┼───▶│  15  │ ●──┼──┐\n└──────┴────┘    └──────┴────┘    └──────┴────┘    └──────┴────┘  │\n  ▲                                                               │\n  └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                the last node links back to the head</code></pre></figure>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-repeat\"></i>Building and traversing</h3>\n<p>The nodes are the same as in a singly linked list; only the last link differs. Traversal must <strong>stop when it comes back to the head</strong>, so the loop prints the head first and then walks until <code>curr == head</code> again. A <code>while curr.next != head</code> loop (as in the original notes) also works but needs the last node printed separately.</p>\n<div class=\"tabs\"><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"Python\"><figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>class Node:\n    def __init__(self, data):\n        self.data = data\n        self.next = None\n\ndef print_circular(head):\n    if head is None:\n        print(\"empty\")\n        return\n    parts = [str(head.data)]\n    curr = head.next\n    while curr != head:              # stop when we are back at the start\n        parts.append(str(curr.data))\n        curr = curr.next\n    print(\" -&gt; \".join(parts), f\"-&gt; (back to {head.data})\")\n\nhead = Node(10)\nhead.next = Node(5)\nhead.next.next = Node(20)\nhead.next.next.next = Node(15)\nhead.next.next.next.next = head      # close the circle\nprint_circular(head)</code></pre></figure></div><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"C++\"><figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\nusing namespace std;\n\nstruct Node {\n    int data; Node* next;\n    Node(int d) : data(d), next(nullptr) {}\n};\n\nvoid printCircular(Node* head) {\n    if (!head) { cout &lt;&lt; \"empty\\n\"; return; }\n    cout &lt;&lt; head-&gt;data;\n    for (Node* curr = head-&gt;next; curr != head; curr = curr-&gt;next)   // stop when back at the start\n        cout &lt;&lt; \" -&gt; \" &lt;&lt; curr-&gt;data;\n    cout &lt;&lt; \" -&gt; (back to \" &lt;&lt; head-&gt;data &lt;&lt; \")\\n\";\n}\n\nint main() {\n    Node* head = new Node(10);\n    head-&gt;next = new Node(5);\n    head-&gt;next-&gt;next = new Node(20);\n    head-&gt;next-&gt;next-&gt;next = new Node(15);\n    head-&gt;next-&gt;next-&gt;next-&gt;next = head;    // close the circle\n    printCircular(head);\n}</code></pre></figure></div><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"Java\"><figure data-lang=\"java\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Java</figcaption><pre><code>public class Main {\n    static class Node {\n        int data; Node next;\n        Node(int d) { data = d; }\n    }\n\n    static void printCircular(Node head) {\n        if (head == null) { System.out.println(\"empty\"); return; }\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder().append(head.data);\n        for (Node curr = head.next; curr != head; curr = curr.next)   // stop when back at the start\n            sb.append(\" -&gt; \").append(curr.data);\n        System.out.println(sb + \" -&gt; (back to \" + head.data + \")\");\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Node head = new Node(10);\n        head.next = new Node(5);\n        head.next.next = new Node(20);\n        head.next.next.next = new Node(15);\n        head.next.next.next.next = head;    // close the circle\n        printCircular(head);\n    }\n}</code></pre></figure></div><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"JavaScript\"><figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>class Node {\n    constructor(data) { this.data = data; this.next = null; }\n}\n\nfunction printCircular(head) {\n    if (head === null) { console.log(\"empty\"); return; }\n    const parts = [head.data];\n    for (let curr = head.next; curr !== head; curr = curr.next)   // stop when back at the start\n        parts.push(curr.data);\n    console.log(parts.join(\" -&gt; \"), `-&gt; (back to ${head.data})`);\n}\n\nconst head = new Node(10);\nhead.next = new Node(5);\nhead.next.next = new Node(20);\nhead.next.next.next = new Node(15);\nhead.next.next.next.next = head;        // close the circle\nprintCircular(head);</code></pre></figure></div></div><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>10 -&gt; 5 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 -&gt; (back to 10)</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"chips\"><span class=\"chip\">Time O(n) traversal</span><span class=\"chip\">Space O(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Pitfall</div><p>A <code>while curr is not None</code> loop never terminates on a circular list. Every traversal must remember where it started and stop there.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-scale\"></i>Advantages and disadvantages</h3>\n<div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-refresh\"></i>Traverse from any node</h3><p>Starting anywhere, following <code>next</code> visits every node — no need to find the head first.</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-clock\"></i>Round-robin scheduling</h3><p>The OS gives each process a time slice and moves to <code>next</code>; after the last process comes the first again. Also: multiplayer turns, circular buffers, music playlists on repeat.</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-bolt\"></i>O(1) at both ends with one pointer</h3><p>Keep a reference to the <strong>tail</strong>: the head is <code>tail.next</code>, so insert at the beginning, insert at the end and delete the head are all O(1).</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-alert-triangle\"></i>More complex code</h3><p>Every operation must handle the empty list, the one-node list (which points at itself) and the wrap-around; an off-by-one gives an infinite loop instead of a crash.</p></div></div>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Operation (holding <code>head</code> only)</th><th>Naive</th><th>Efficient trick</th><th>Holding <code>tail</code> instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Insert at beginning</td><td>O(n): walk to the last node to fix its <code>next</code></td><td>O(1): insert <em>after</em> head and swap data</td><td>O(1)</td></tr><tr><td>Insert at end</td><td>O(n): walk to the last node</td><td>O(1): same trick, return the new node as head</td><td>O(1)</td></tr><tr><td>Delete head</td><td>O(n): walk to the last node to re-point it</td><td>O(1): copy <code>head.next</code> into head and unlink <code>head.next</code></td><td>O(1)</td></tr><tr><td>Delete k-th node</td><td>O(k)</td><td>—</td><td>O(k)</td></tr><tr><td>Search</td><td>O(n)</td><td>—</td><td>O(n)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrow-bar-to-left\"></i>Insert at the beginning</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Example</div><p><strong>Input:</strong> <code>list = 10 -&gt; 5 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 (circular), insert 25 at the beginning</code><br><strong>Output:</strong> <code>25 -&gt; 10 -&gt; 5 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 -&gt; (back to 25)</code></p></div>\n<p><strong>Naive, O(n).</strong> The last node must point at the new head, and the only way to reach the last node is to walk the whole circle.</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>class Node:\n    def __init__(self, data):\n        self.data = data\n        self.next = None\n\ndef insert_beginning_naive(head, x):\n    temp = Node(x)\n    if head is None:\n        temp.next = temp               # one node points at itself\n        return temp\n    curr = head\n    while curr.next != head:           # O(n) walk to the last node\n        curr = curr.next\n    curr.next = temp                   # last node → new node\n    temp.next = head                   # new node → old head\n    return temp\n\ndef print_circular(head):\n    parts, curr = [str(head.data)], head.next\n    while curr != head:\n        parts.append(str(curr.data)); curr = curr.next\n    print(\" -&gt; \".join(parts), f\"-&gt; (back to {head.data})\")\n\nhead = Node(10); head.next = Node(5); head.next.next = Node(20); head.next.next.next = Node(15)\nhead.next.next.next.next = head\nhead = insert_beginning_naive(head, 25)\nprint_circular(head)</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>25 -&gt; 10 -&gt; 5 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 -&gt; (back to 25)</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"chips\"><span class=\"chip\">Time O(n)</span><span class=\"chip\">Space O(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Idea</div><p><strong>Efficient, O(1).</strong> Insert the new node <em>right after</em> the head (two pointer changes — no walk) and then <strong>swap the data</strong> of the head and the new node. The head node now carries the new value and the old head value sits in second position: exactly the result of inserting at the front. The head reference does not even change.</p></div>\n<figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Insert at the beginning in O(1): insert after the head, then swap the two values</figcaption><pre><code>before:          head ──▶ [10] ──▶ [5] ──▶ [20] ──▶ [15] ──▶ back to 10\ninsert after head:   head ──▶ [10] ──▶ [25] ──▶ [5] ──▶ [20] ──▶ [15] ──▶ back to 10\nswap data:           head ──▶ [25] ──▶ [10] ──▶ [5] ──▶ [20] ──▶ [15] ──▶ back to 25</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"tabs\"><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"Python\"><figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>class Node:\n    def __init__(self, data):\n        self.data = data\n        self.next = None\n\ndef insert_beginning(head, x):\n    temp = Node(x)\n    if head is None:\n        temp.next = temp                             # one node points at itself\n        return temp\n    temp.next = head.next                            # insert temp right after head\n    head.next = temp\n    head.data, temp.data = temp.data, head.data      # swap values: head now holds x\n    return head\n\ndef print_circular(head):\n    parts, curr = [str(head.data)], head.next\n    while curr != head:\n        parts.append(str(curr.data)); curr = curr.next\n    print(\" -&gt; \".join(parts), f\"-&gt; (back to {head.data})\")\n\nhead = Node(10); head.next = Node(5); head.next.next = Node(20); head.next.next.next = Node(15)\nhead.next.next.next.next = head\nhead = insert_beginning(head, 25); print_circular(head)\nhead = insert_beginning(head, 30); print_circular(head)</code></pre></figure></div><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"C++\"><figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;utility&gt;\nusing namespace std;\n\nstruct Node {\n    int data; Node* next;\n    Node(int d) : data(d), next(nullptr) {}\n};\n\nNode* insertBeginning(Node* head, int x) {\n    Node* temp = new Node(x);\n    if (!head) { temp-&gt;next = temp; return temp; }   // one node points at itself\n    temp-&gt;next = head-&gt;next;                         // insert temp right after head\n    head-&gt;next = temp;\n    swap(head-&gt;data, temp-&gt;data);                    // swap values: head now holds x\n    return head;\n}\n\nvoid printCircular(Node* head) {\n    cout &lt;&lt; head-&gt;data;\n    for (Node* curr = head-&gt;next; curr != head; curr = curr-&gt;next) cout &lt;&lt; \" -&gt; \" &lt;&lt; curr-&gt;data;\n    cout &lt;&lt; \" -&gt; (back to \" &lt;&lt; head-&gt;data &lt;&lt; \")\\n\";\n}\n\nint main() {\n    Node* head = new Node(10); head-&gt;next = new Node(5); head-&gt;next-&gt;next = new Node(20);\n    head-&gt;next-&gt;next-&gt;next = new Node(15); head-&gt;next-&gt;next-&gt;next-&gt;next = head;\n    head = insertBeginning(head, 25); printCircular(head);\n    head = insertBeginning(head, 30); printCircular(head);\n}</code></pre></figure></div><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"Java\"><figure data-lang=\"java\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Java</figcaption><pre><code>public class Main {\n    static class Node {\n        int data; Node next;\n        Node(int d) { data = d; }\n    }\n\n    static Node insertBeginning(Node head, int x) {\n        Node temp = new Node(x);\n        if (head == null) { temp.next = temp; return temp; }   // one node points at itself\n        temp.next = head.next;                                  // insert temp right after head\n        head.next = temp;\n        int t = head.data; head.data = temp.data; temp.data = t; // swap values: head now holds x\n        return head;\n    }\n\n    static void printCircular(Node head) {\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder().append(head.data);\n        for (Node curr = head.next; curr != head; curr = curr.next) sb.append(\" -&gt; \").append(curr.data);\n        System.out.println(sb + \" -&gt; (back to \" + head.data + \")\");\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Node head = new Node(10); head.next = new Node(5); head.next.next = new Node(20);\n        head.next.next.next = new Node(15); head.next.next.next.next = head;\n        head = insertBeginning(head, 25); printCircular(head);\n        head = insertBeginning(head, 30); printCircular(head);\n    }\n}</code></pre></figure></div><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"JavaScript\"><figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>class Node {\n    constructor(data) { this.data = data; this.next = null; }\n}\n\nfunction insertBeginning(head, x) {\n    const temp = new Node(x);\n    if (head === null) { temp.next = temp; return temp; }   // one node points at itself\n    temp.next = head.next;                                   // insert temp right after head\n    head.next = temp;\n    [head.data, temp.data] = [temp.data, head.data];         // swap values: head now holds x\n    return head;\n}\n\nfunction printCircular(head) {\n    const parts = [head.data];\n    for (let curr = head.next; curr !== head; curr = curr.next) parts.push(curr.data);\n    console.log(parts.join(\" -&gt; \"), `-&gt; (back to ${head.data})`);\n}\n\nlet head = new Node(10); head.next = new Node(5); head.next.next = new Node(20);\nhead.next.next.next = new Node(15); head.next.next.next.next = head;\nhead = insertBeginning(head, 25); printCircular(head);\nhead = insertBeginning(head, 30); printCircular(head);</code></pre></figure></div></div><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>25 -&gt; 10 -&gt; 5 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 -&gt; (back to 25)\n30 -&gt; 25 -&gt; 10 -&gt; 5 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 -&gt; (back to 30)</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"chips\"><span class=\"chip\">Time O(1)</span><span class=\"chip\">Space O(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Pitfall</div><p>The swap trick moves a <em>value</em> into a different node. If other code holds references to specific nodes (or the data is large/expensive to copy), use the tail-pointer design instead: with <code>tail</code> known, <code>head = tail.next</code> and both ends are O(1) without any swapping.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrow-bar-to-right\"></i>Insert at the end</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Example</div><p><strong>Input:</strong> <code>list = 10 -&gt; 5 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 (circular), insert 35 at the end</code><br><strong>Output:</strong> <code>10 -&gt; 5 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 -&gt; 35 -&gt; (back to 10)</code></p></div>\n<p><strong>Naive, O(n).</strong> Walk to the last node, link it to the new node and link the new node back to the head.</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>class Node:\n    def __init__(self, data):\n        self.data = data\n        self.next = None\n\ndef insert_end_naive(head, x):\n    temp = Node(x)\n    if head is None:\n        temp.next = temp\n        return temp\n    curr = head\n    while curr.next != head:           # O(n) walk to the last node\n        curr = curr.next\n    curr.next = temp                   # last → new\n    temp.next = head                   # new → head\n    return head\n\ndef print_circular(head):\n    parts, curr = [str(head.data)], head.next\n    while curr != head:\n        parts.append(str(curr.data)); curr = curr.next\n    print(\" -&gt; \".join(parts), f\"-&gt; (back to {head.data})\")\n\nhead = Node(10); head.next = Node(5); head.next.next = Node(20); head.next.next.next = Node(15)\nhead.next.next.next.next = head\nhead = insert_end_naive(head, 35)\nprint_circular(head)</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>10 -&gt; 5 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 -&gt; 35 -&gt; (back to 10)</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"chips\"><span class=\"chip\">Time O(n)</span><span class=\"chip\">Space O(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Idea</div><p><strong>Efficient, O(1).</strong> Same trick as before — insert the new node after the head and swap the values — but now <strong>return the new node as the head</strong>. Reading the circle from that node gives the old sequence first and the new value last: the head node (which now holds <code>x</code>) comes just before it.</p></div>\n<div class=\"tabs\"><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"Python\"><figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>class Node:\n    def __init__(self, data):\n        self.data = data\n        self.next = None\n\ndef insert_end(head, x):\n    temp = Node(x)\n    if head is None:\n        temp.next = temp\n        return temp\n    temp.next = head.next                            # insert temp right after head\n    head.next = temp\n    head.data, temp.data = temp.data, head.data      # old head value moves to temp\n    return temp                                      # temp is the new head; x sits just before it\n\ndef print_circular(head):\n    parts, curr = [str(head.data)], head.next\n    while curr != head:\n        parts.append(str(curr.data)); curr = curr.next\n    print(\" -&gt; \".join(parts), f\"-&gt; (back to {head.data})\")\n\nhead = Node(10); head.next = Node(5); head.next.next = Node(20); head.next.next.next = Node(15)\nhead.next.next.next.next = head\nhead = insert_end(head, 35); print_circular(head)\nhead = insert_end(head, 40); print_circular(head)</code></pre></figure></div><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"C++\"><figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\n#include &lt;utility&gt;\nusing namespace std;\n\nstruct Node {\n    int data; Node* next;\n    Node(int d) : data(d), next(nullptr) {}\n};\n\nNode* insertEnd(Node* head, int x) {\n    Node* temp = new Node(x);\n    if (!head) { temp-&gt;next = temp; return temp; }\n    temp-&gt;next = head-&gt;next;                         // insert temp right after head\n    head-&gt;next = temp;\n    swap(head-&gt;data, temp-&gt;data);                    // old head value moves to temp\n    return temp;                                     // temp is the new head; x sits just before it\n}\n\nvoid printCircular(Node* head) {\n    cout &lt;&lt; head-&gt;data;\n    for (Node* curr = head-&gt;next; curr != head; curr = curr-&gt;next) cout &lt;&lt; \" -&gt; \" &lt;&lt; curr-&gt;data;\n    cout &lt;&lt; \" -&gt; (back to \" &lt;&lt; head-&gt;data &lt;&lt; \")\\n\";\n}\n\nint main() {\n    Node* head = new Node(10); head-&gt;next = new Node(5); head-&gt;next-&gt;next = new Node(20);\n    head-&gt;next-&gt;next-&gt;next = new Node(15); head-&gt;next-&gt;next-&gt;next-&gt;next = head;\n    head = insertEnd(head, 35); printCircular(head);\n    head = insertEnd(head, 40); printCircular(head);\n}</code></pre></figure></div><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"Java\"><figure data-lang=\"java\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Java</figcaption><pre><code>public class Main {\n    static class Node {\n        int data; Node next;\n        Node(int d) { data = d; }\n    }\n\n    static Node insertEnd(Node head, int x) {\n        Node temp = new Node(x);\n        if (head == null) { temp.next = temp; return temp; }\n        temp.next = head.next;                                   // insert temp right after head\n        head.next = temp;\n        int t = head.data; head.data = temp.data; temp.data = t;  // old head value moves to temp\n        return temp;                                             // temp is the new head; x sits just before it\n    }\n\n    static void printCircular(Node head) {\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder().append(head.data);\n        for (Node curr = head.next; curr != head; curr = curr.next) sb.append(\" -&gt; \").append(curr.data);\n        System.out.println(sb + \" -&gt; (back to \" + head.data + \")\");\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Node head = new Node(10); head.next = new Node(5); head.next.next = new Node(20);\n        head.next.next.next = new Node(15); head.next.next.next.next = head;\n        head = insertEnd(head, 35); printCircular(head);\n        head = insertEnd(head, 40); printCircular(head);\n    }\n}</code></pre></figure></div><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"JavaScript\"><figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>class Node {\n    constructor(data) { this.data = data; this.next = null; }\n}\n\nfunction insertEnd(head, x) {\n    const temp = new Node(x);\n    if (head === null) { temp.next = temp; return temp; }\n    temp.next = head.next;                                   // insert temp right after head\n    head.next = temp;\n    [head.data, temp.data] = [temp.data, head.data];         // old head value moves to temp\n    return temp;                                             // temp is the new head; x sits just before it\n}\n\nfunction printCircular(head) {\n    const parts = [head.data];\n    for (let curr = head.next; curr !== head; curr = curr.next) parts.push(curr.data);\n    console.log(parts.join(\" -&gt; \"), `-&gt; (back to ${head.data})`);\n}\n\nlet head = new Node(10); head.next = new Node(5); head.next.next = new Node(20);\nhead.next.next.next = new Node(15); head.next.next.next.next = head;\nhead = insertEnd(head, 35); printCircular(head);\nhead = insertEnd(head, 40); printCircular(head);</code></pre></figure></div></div><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>10 -&gt; 5 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 -&gt; 35 -&gt; (back to 10)\n10 -&gt; 5 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 -&gt; 35 -&gt; 40 -&gt; (back to 10)</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"chips\"><span class=\"chip\">Time O(1)</span><span class=\"chip\">Space O(1)</span></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-arrow-bar-left\"></i>Delete the head</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Example</div><p><strong>Input:</strong> <code>list = 10 -&gt; 5 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 (circular)</code><br><strong>Output:</strong> <code>5 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 -&gt; (back to 5)</code><br><strong>Input:</strong> <code>list = 10 (one node)</code><br><strong>Output:</strong> <code>empty</code></p></div>\n<p><strong>Naive, O(n).</strong> The last node points at the head, so after removing the head the last node must be found and re-pointed at the second node — a full walk.</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>class Node:\n    def __init__(self, data):\n        self.data = data\n        self.next = None\n\ndef delete_head_naive(head):\n    if head is None or head.next == head:   # empty or single node → empty\n        return None\n    curr = head\n    while curr.next != head:                # O(n) walk to the last node\n        curr = curr.next\n    curr.next = head.next                   # last → second node\n    return curr.next                        # second node is the new head\n\ndef print_circular(head):\n    parts, curr = [str(head.data)], head.next\n    while curr != head:\n        parts.append(str(curr.data)); curr = curr.next\n    print(\" -&gt; \".join(parts), f\"-&gt; (back to {head.data})\")\n\nhead = Node(10); head.next = Node(5); head.next.next = Node(20); head.next.next.next = Node(15)\nhead.next.next.next.next = head\nhead = delete_head_naive(head)\nprint_circular(head)</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>5 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 -&gt; (back to 5)</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"chips\"><span class=\"chip\">Time O(n)</span><span class=\"chip\">Space O(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Idea</div><p><strong>Efficient, O(1).</strong> Instead of removing the head node, <strong>copy the second node's value into it</strong> and unlink the second node. The head node object survives, so the last node's back-pointer stays valid without any walk.</p></div>\n<div class=\"tabs\"><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"Python\"><figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>class Node:\n    def __init__(self, data):\n        self.data = data\n        self.next = None\n\ndef delete_head(head):\n    if head is None or head.next == head:   # empty or single node → empty\n        return None\n    head.data = head.next.data               # pull the second value into the head node\n    head.next = head.next.next               # unlink the second node\n    return head\n\ndef print_circular(head):\n    if head is None:\n        print(\"empty\"); return\n    parts, curr = [str(head.data)], head.next\n    while curr != head:\n        parts.append(str(curr.data)); curr = curr.next\n    print(\" -&gt; \".join(parts), f\"-&gt; (back to {head.data})\")\n\nhead = Node(10); head.next = Node(5); head.next.next = Node(20); head.next.next.next = Node(15)\nhead.next.next.next.next = head\nfor _ in range(4):\n    head = delete_head(head)\n    print_circular(head)</code></pre></figure></div><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"C++\"><figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\nusing namespace std;\n\nstruct Node {\n    int data; Node* next;\n    Node(int d) : data(d), next(nullptr) {}\n};\n\nNode* deleteHead(Node* head) {\n    if (!head) return nullptr;\n    if (head-&gt;next == head) { delete head; return nullptr; }   // single node → empty\n    Node* second = head-&gt;next;\n    head-&gt;data = second-&gt;data;               // pull the second value into the head node\n    head-&gt;next = second-&gt;next;               // unlink the second node\n    delete second;\n    return head;\n}\n\nvoid printCircular(Node* head) {\n    if (!head) { cout &lt;&lt; \"empty\\n\"; return; }\n    cout &lt;&lt; head-&gt;data;\n    for (Node* curr = head-&gt;next; curr != head; curr = curr-&gt;next) cout &lt;&lt; \" -&gt; \" &lt;&lt; curr-&gt;data;\n    cout &lt;&lt; \" -&gt; (back to \" &lt;&lt; head-&gt;data &lt;&lt; \")\\n\";\n}\n\nint main() {\n    Node* head = new Node(10); head-&gt;next = new Node(5); head-&gt;next-&gt;next = new Node(20);\n    head-&gt;next-&gt;next-&gt;next = new Node(15); head-&gt;next-&gt;next-&gt;next-&gt;next = head;\n    for (int i = 0; i &lt; 4; i++) {\n        head = deleteHead(head);\n        printCircular(head);\n    }\n}</code></pre></figure></div><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"Java\"><figure data-lang=\"java\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Java</figcaption><pre><code>public class Main {\n    static class Node {\n        int data; Node next;\n        Node(int d) { data = d; }\n    }\n\n    static Node deleteHead(Node head) {\n        if (head == null || head.next == head) return null;   // empty or single node → empty\n        head.data = head.next.data;              // pull the second value into the head node\n        head.next = head.next.next;              // unlink the second node\n        return head;\n    }\n\n    static void printCircular(Node head) {\n        if (head == null) { System.out.println(\"empty\"); return; }\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder().append(head.data);\n        for (Node curr = head.next; curr != head; curr = curr.next) sb.append(\" -&gt; \").append(curr.data);\n        System.out.println(sb + \" -&gt; (back to \" + head.data + \")\");\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Node head = new Node(10); head.next = new Node(5); head.next.next = new Node(20);\n        head.next.next.next = new Node(15); head.next.next.next.next = head;\n        for (int i = 0; i &lt; 4; i++) {\n            head = deleteHead(head);\n            printCircular(head);\n        }\n    }\n}</code></pre></figure></div><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"JavaScript\"><figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>class Node {\n    constructor(data) { this.data = data; this.next = null; }\n}\n\nfunction deleteHead(head) {\n    if (head === null || head.next === head) return null;    // empty or single node → empty\n    head.data = head.next.data;                  // pull the second value into the head node\n    head.next = head.next.next;                  // unlink the second node\n    return head;\n}\n\nfunction printCircular(head) {\n    if (head === null) { console.log(\"empty\"); return; }\n    const parts = [head.data];\n    for (let curr = head.next; curr !== head; curr = curr.next) parts.push(curr.data);\n    console.log(parts.join(\" -&gt; \"), `-&gt; (back to ${head.data})`);\n}\n\nlet head = new Node(10); head.next = new Node(5); head.next.next = new Node(20);\nhead.next.next.next = new Node(15); head.next.next.next.next = head;\nfor (let i = 0; i &lt; 4; i++) {\n    head = deleteHead(head);\n    printCircular(head);\n}</code></pre></figure></div></div><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>5 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 -&gt; (back to 5)\n20 -&gt; 15 -&gt; (back to 20)\n15 -&gt; (back to 15)\nempty</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"chips\"><span class=\"chip\">Time O(1)</span><span class=\"chip\">Space O(1)</span></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-list-numbers\"></i>Delete the k-th node</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Example</div><p><strong>Input:</strong> <code>list = 10 -&gt; 5 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 (circular), k = 2</code><br><strong>Output:</strong> <code>10 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 -&gt; (back to 10)</code><br><strong>Input:</strong> <code>k = 1</code><br><strong>Output:</strong> <code>5 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 -&gt; (back to 5)</code></p></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Idea</div><p><code>k = 1</code> is the head — reuse <code>delete_head</code>. Otherwise walk to the <code>(k-1)</code>-th node, which takes <code>k - 2</code> steps from the head, and bypass its successor: <code>curr.next = curr.next.next</code>. The circle stays closed because the bypassed node's <code>next</code> is reused.</p></div>\n<div class=\"step\"><div class=\"step-num\">1</div><div class=\"step-body\"><div class=\"step-title\">Empty list</div><div class=\"step-desc\">Return <code>None</code>.</div></div></div><div class=\"step\"><div class=\"step-num\">2</div><div class=\"step-body\"><div class=\"step-title\"><code>k == 1</code></div><div class=\"step-desc\">Return <code>delete_head(head)</code> — the O(1) version above.</div></div></div><div class=\"step\"><div class=\"step-num\">3</div><div class=\"step-body\"><div class=\"step-title\">Walk</div><div class=\"step-desc\"><code>curr = head</code>; move <code>k - 2</code> times → <code>curr</code> is the <code>(k-1)</code>-th node.</div></div></div><div class=\"step\"><div class=\"step-num\">4</div><div class=\"step-body\"><div class=\"step-title\">Bypass</div><div class=\"step-desc\"><code>curr.next = curr.next.next</code> removes the <code>k</code>-th node.</div></div></div>\n<div class=\"tabs\"><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"Python\"><figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>class Node:\n    def __init__(self, data):\n        self.data = data\n        self.next = None\n\ndef delete_head(head):\n    if head is None or head.next == head:\n        return None\n    head.data = head.next.data\n    head.next = head.next.next\n    return head\n\ndef delete_kth(head, k):\n    if head is None:\n        return None\n    if k == 1:\n        return delete_head(head)\n    curr = head\n    for _ in range(k - 2):                   # k-2 steps reach the (k-1)-th node\n        curr = curr.next\n    curr.next = curr.next.next               # bypass the k-th node\n    return head\n\ndef print_circular(head):\n    parts, curr = [str(head.data)], head.next\n    while curr != head:\n        parts.append(str(curr.data)); curr = curr.next\n    print(\" -&gt; \".join(parts), f\"-&gt; (back to {head.data})\")\n\nhead = Node(10); head.next = Node(5); head.next.next = Node(20); head.next.next.next = Node(15)\nhead.next.next.next.next = head\nprint_circular(head)\nfor k, label in ((2, \"2nd\"), (3, \"3rd\"), (1, \"1st\")):\n    head = delete_kth(head, k)\n    print(f\"delete {label}: \", end=\"\"); print_circular(head)</code></pre></figure></div><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"C++\"><figure data-lang=\"cpp\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>C++</figcaption><pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;\nusing namespace std;\n\nstruct Node {\n    int data; Node* next;\n    Node(int d) : data(d), next(nullptr) {}\n};\n\nNode* deleteHead(Node* head) {\n    if (!head) return nullptr;\n    if (head-&gt;next == head) { delete head; return nullptr; }\n    Node* second = head-&gt;next;\n    head-&gt;data = second-&gt;data; head-&gt;next = second-&gt;next;\n    delete second;\n    return head;\n}\n\nNode* deleteKth(Node* head, int k) {\n    if (!head) return nullptr;\n    if (k == 1) return deleteHead(head);\n    Node* curr = head;\n    for (int i = 0; i &lt; k - 2; i++) curr = curr-&gt;next;   // k-2 steps reach the (k-1)-th node\n    Node* victim = curr-&gt;next;\n    curr-&gt;next = victim-&gt;next;                           // bypass the k-th node\n    delete victim;\n    return head;\n}\n\nvoid printCircular(Node* head) {\n    cout &lt;&lt; head-&gt;data;\n    for (Node* curr = head-&gt;next; curr != head; curr = curr-&gt;next) cout &lt;&lt; \" -&gt; \" &lt;&lt; curr-&gt;data;\n    cout &lt;&lt; \" -&gt; (back to \" &lt;&lt; head-&gt;data &lt;&lt; \")\\n\";\n}\n\nint main() {\n    Node* head = new Node(10); head-&gt;next = new Node(5); head-&gt;next-&gt;next = new Node(20);\n    head-&gt;next-&gt;next-&gt;next = new Node(15); head-&gt;next-&gt;next-&gt;next-&gt;next = head;\n    printCircular(head);\n    int ks[] = {2, 3, 1}; const char* labels[] = {\"2nd\", \"3rd\", \"1st\"};\n    for (int i = 0; i &lt; 3; i++) {\n        head = deleteKth(head, ks[i]);\n        cout &lt;&lt; \"delete \" &lt;&lt; labels[i] &lt;&lt; \": \"; printCircular(head);\n    }\n}</code></pre></figure></div><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"Java\"><figure data-lang=\"java\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Java</figcaption><pre><code>public class Main {\n    static class Node {\n        int data; Node next;\n        Node(int d) { data = d; }\n    }\n\n    static Node deleteHead(Node head) {\n        if (head == null || head.next == head) return null;\n        head.data = head.next.data; head.next = head.next.next;\n        return head;\n    }\n\n    static Node deleteKth(Node head, int k) {\n        if (head == null) return null;\n        if (k == 1) return deleteHead(head);\n        Node curr = head;\n        for (int i = 0; i &lt; k - 2; i++) curr = curr.next;   // k-2 steps reach the (k-1)-th node\n        curr.next = curr.next.next;                         // bypass the k-th node\n        return head;\n    }\n\n    static void printCircular(Node head) {\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder().append(head.data);\n        for (Node curr = head.next; curr != head; curr = curr.next) sb.append(\" -&gt; \").append(curr.data);\n        System.out.println(sb + \" -&gt; (back to \" + head.data + \")\");\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Node head = new Node(10); head.next = new Node(5); head.next.next = new Node(20);\n        head.next.next.next = new Node(15); head.next.next.next.next = head;\n        printCircular(head);\n        int[] ks = {2, 3, 1}; String[] labels = {\"2nd\", \"3rd\", \"1st\"};\n        for (int i = 0; i &lt; 3; i++) {\n            head = deleteKth(head, ks[i]);\n            System.out.print(\"delete \" + labels[i] + \": \"); printCircular(head);\n        }\n    }\n}</code></pre></figure></div><div class=\"tab-panel\" data-label=\"JavaScript\"><figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>class Node {\n    constructor(data) { this.data = data; this.next = null; }\n}\n\nfunction deleteHead(head) {\n    if (head === null || head.next === head) return null;\n    head.data = head.next.data; head.next = head.next.next;\n    return head;\n}\n\nfunction deleteKth(head, k) {\n    if (head === null) return null;\n    if (k === 1) return deleteHead(head);\n    let curr = head;\n    for (let i = 0; i &lt; k - 2; i++) curr = curr.next;   // k-2 steps reach the (k-1)-th node\n    curr.next = curr.next.next;                         // bypass the k-th node\n    return head;\n}\n\nfunction printCircular(head) {\n    const parts = [head.data];\n    for (let curr = head.next; curr !== head; curr = curr.next) parts.push(curr.data);\n    console.log(parts.join(\" -&gt; \"), `-&gt; (back to ${head.data})`);\n}\n\nlet head = new Node(10); head.next = new Node(5); head.next.next = new Node(20);\nhead.next.next.next = new Node(15); head.next.next.next.next = head;\nprintCircular(head);\nfor (const [k, label] of [[2, \"2nd\"], [3, \"3rd\"], [1, \"1st\"]]) {\n    head = deleteKth(head, k);\n    process.stdout.write(`delete ${label}: `); printCircular(head);\n}</code></pre></figure></div></div><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>10 -&gt; 5 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 -&gt; (back to 10)\ndelete 2nd: 10 -&gt; 20 -&gt; 15 -&gt; (back to 10)\ndelete 3rd: 10 -&gt; 20 -&gt; (back to 10)\ndelete 1st: 20 -&gt; (back to 20)</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"chips\"><span class=\"chip\">Time O(k)</span><span class=\"chip\">Space O(1)</span></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Pitfall</div><p>The original notes looped <code>for i in range(1, k-2)</code>, which takes <code>k - 3</code> steps and deletes the wrong node for every <code>k &gt; 2</code>. Count the steps on paper: from node 1, reaching node <code>k-1</code> is exactly <code>k - 2</code> hops. The code also assumes <code>k ≤ length</code>; add a length check (or stop when <code>curr.next == head</code>) for untrusted input.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-message-question\"></i>Interview Q&amp;A</h3>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>How do you detect that a linked list is circular?</summary><div><p>Traverse with a <code>fast</code> pointer moving two steps and a <code>slow</code> pointer moving one (Floyd's cycle detection). In a circular list they eventually meet; in a normal list <code>fast</code> reaches <code>None</code>. O(n) time, O(1) space — a visited-set would also work but costs O(n) memory.</p></div></details>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Why keep a tail pointer rather than a head pointer in a circular list?</summary><div><p>Because <code>tail.next</code> <em>is</em> the head. With the tail you can insert at the front (<code>new.next = tail.next; tail.next = new</code>), insert at the back (same, then <code>tail = new</code>) and delete the front, all in O(1), without the value-swapping trick. Queues built on circular lists do exactly this.</p></div></details>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Where are circular linked lists used in practice?</summary><div><p>Round-robin CPU scheduling, turn order in games, circular buffers for streaming data, Fibonacci heaps (the root list is circular doubly linked), and the Josephus problem — every k-th person around a circle is eliminated until one remains.</p></div></details>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>What goes wrong if you forget the single-node case?</summary><div><p>A one-node circular list has <code>head.next == head</code>. A <code>delete_head</code> that does <code>head.next = head.next.next</code> would leave the node pointing at itself and return it — the list never becomes empty. Always test the empty, one-node and two-node lists.</p></div></details></section>"}